title: date
location: ship deck
---

Tsuru has coordinated two teams of officers to set sail on her pink-sailed warship.
On deck, you discuss the strategy with her.
-> I don't think that we will make it on time.
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: Don't you trust me, {$name}?
    Tsuru: We will sail over a very fast current that runs parallel to the Red Line.
    Tsuru: The pirates won't know we are coming.
-> What do we know about the pirates until now?
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: Very good question.
    Tsuru: These are the Nemo Pirates. A crew powerful enough to have multiple ships under their command.
-> I'll await your orders!
    Tsuru: Thank you, {$name}. Let me think.
Tsuru: They might be looking for ransom...
Tsuru: All men to their positions!
Tsuru's ship creaks and groans in the current. A cutting wind hits the sails while, all around you, boots storm around the ship. The open sea at your left, Red Line on the right side. This is going faster than you imagined.
You glance at Tsuru. Arms crossed, coat waving in the wind, nothing can rattle her. She's incredible!
Tsuru: We are getting closer to—
Tsuru: I need to know that you are OK with this, {$name}. We have two warships, so I won't involve you in the fighting unless it's absolutely necessary... If you don't want to, that is.
-> No, we should go ahead and attack them all-out!
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: Don't be irresponsible! We still know too little about the situation.
    Tsuru: You're sounding like Garp...
-> I think we should approach the enemy carefully. Let's send only one of the ships first.
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: That is a good idea... That way, the enemy will think that we only dispatched one ship.
    Tsuru: That is assuming none of them use Haki.
    -> I'll fetch that information for you!
        <<set td4_points +=1>>
        Tsuru: Thank you, {$name}.
    -> Oh, I'm sure they don't!
        Tsuru: I'll find out for sure.
    -> I'm fine with going or with staying here. Whatever we need!
        Tsuru: Very well.
You see lights and hear swords clashing in the distance. Or is it a trick of the wind?
Tsuru speaks into her transponder snail.
Tsuru: Go ahead and speed ahead of us!
Tsuru: Do you see those lights in the distance, {$name}?
-> Let's go after them immediately! What if it's a distress signal from our men?
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: Don't act on an impulse.
    Tsuru: It might be the pirates communicating with each other... Or trying to trick us.
-> It seems like a Navy signal, but it's hard to tell.
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: Very true.
    Tsuru: It might be a trick, or the pirates communicating with each other... Let's wait for our officers to assess the attack.
In the distance, cannons thunder.
Snail: Some pirates are aboard the Navy vessel and attempting to take control! The other pirates are trying to flee.
-> How are the officers holding up?
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: That is the right question.
    Tsuru repeats it into the snail.
    Snail: With a few reinforcements, it should be possible to win control over the vessel!
    Tsuru: That is fine. We have sent a ship in their direction already.
-> We must help the officers! Let's sail directly into the battle.
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: {$name}, our officers should be able to hold a grip on their ship.
    Tsuru: In case they don't, we have already sent reinforcements.
-> The officers should be fine. Let's circle the battle and capture all the remaining pirates.
    Tsuru: That is quite the bold thing to say, {$name}.
    Tsuru speaks into the snail.
    Tsuru: How are the officers holding up?
    Snail: With a few reinforcements, it should be possible to win control over the vessel!
Tsuru: OK, this is the time to decide.
Tsuru: Should we barge into the battle, or circle it and make more captures?
-> Into the battle!
    <<jump date_tsuru_4_ship_end_neutral>>
-> Make captures!
    <<set td4_points +=2>>
    <<jump date_tsuru_4_ship_end_good>>
===

title: date_tsuru_4_ship_end_neutral
location: ship deck
---

Tsuru's ship thumps forward with a roar of its Dial system, and the ships — enemy and Navy — grow in the distance! Officers scramble to the cannons, landing a few shots around the enemy vessel that is attempting to flee. It's all very confusing in this cloud of smoke.
Tsuru: Now. We're reclaiming our own ship!
Once you're close enough, Tsuru intercepts the Navy ship and boards it, taking the pirates by surprise.
There's a crowd of pirates shouting about how *pure and cleansed* they now feel after Tsuru's intervention! But the rest have fled...
Once the fight has settled down and arrests have been made, Tsuru turns to you.
Tsuru: Well... It was worth a try, {$name}. But there were no big losses.
Tsuru: Thank you for your help.
-> You're welcome!
    Tsuru: And... Thanks for your understanding, too.
-> Are we going to pick up where we left it off sometime?
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru chuckles.
    Tsuru: I'd love to.
    Tsuru smiles and holds your hand.
    <<jump date_tsuru_4_Date_Ends>>
===

title: date_tsuru_4_ship_end_good
location: ship deck
---

With a roar of the Dial system and a mighty creak, Tsuru's warship turns forward, making a long ‘U' around the battlezone.
Officers scramble to the cannons and shoot. A cloud of gunpowder and smoke thickens the air, confusing the enemy.
Once you're close enough, Tsuru intercepts the fleeing pirate ship.
From the Navy deck, officers shoot at the unprepared crew.
Tsuru can repel any attacks that come her way with Haki. Unafraid, she orders her crew to get closer until she can board the enemy ship.
It's a victory!
Once the battle has settled down and arrests have been made, Tsuru turns to you.
Tsuru: Well, this was an unexpected end to the evening.
-> It was awesome!
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: Well... That's a strange way to talk about battle...
    Tsuru: I suppose I'm glad you had fun...
-> Well, not what we were expecting, but it was OK...
    Tsuru: And... Thanks for your understanding, too.
- {$name} Are we going to pick up where we left it off sometime? <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru chuckles.
    Tsuru: I'd love to.
She smiles, holding your hand in hers.
<<jump date_tsuru_4_Date_Ends>>
===

title: date_tsuru_4_no_snail
location: town
---

You make your way to the New Marineford town. It's Friday, and the night is warm and breezy. The night lights and busy streets make for a comfortable atmosphere.
There's still a little bit of time left.
{$name}: Hmmm... Should I pick Tsuru up close to her home?
{$name}: I can't make any calls, so I can't ask if that is OK with her.
-> Pick her up
    <<jump date_tsuru_4_no_snail_home>>
-> Go to the theater directly
    <<jump date_tsuru_4_no_snail_queue>>
===

title: date_tsuru_4_no_snail_home
location: town
---

It takes a few minutes to get there on foot. Tsuru lives in a nice, quaint house in a quiet corner of town. It is surrounded by a gate, thick with ivy; there is a pond, a birdhouse, and a few plants in beautiful pots. Warm light pours out through the patterned window curtains.
She has obviously put care into making her home cozy. You ring the bell...
Tsuru answers, nicely dressed.
Tsuru: Ah! {$name}.
-> You look beautiful!
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: Thank you, but...
    Tsuru: I wish you had called earlier.
    -> I'm sorry, I couldn't wait.
        <<set td4_points +=1>>
        Tsuru: I understand.
        Tsuru: Well, then. Please come in. And excuse the mess!
    -> Oh, I'll just wait outside, then!
        Tsuru: I know you're not serious about that, {$name}.
        Tsuru: Please, come in. And excuse the mess!
-> I hope it's OK that I came here first!
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: ...Well, I do wish you had called, {$name}. I find it easier to plan in advance.
    Tsuru: Ah... It's not a big issue.
    Tsuru: Please, come in. And excuse the mess.
You accept her invitation, although you struggle to get what she means by “mess”! The entrance looks quite traditional, with a small pond and few plants in beautiful pots. She obviously puts care into making a warm impression.
There's a white cat in the corner, meowing at you. It has a purple star-shaped mark over its eye.
Tsuru: Oh, that's Yuki.
-> Here, kitty kitty...
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    You try to approach, but the cat hisses at you.
    Tsuru: Ah, excuse her, {$name}... Sometimes she is afraid of new faces.
    Yuki's tail sways in the air.
    -> This must mean she likes me!
        <<set td4_points -=1>>
    -> I think she's still undecided...
-> Can I pet her?
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    The cat meows, but looks at you warily.
    Tsuru: Ah... Maybe let her approach you first, {$name}.
    Yuki's tail sways.
    -> Maybe she likes me!
    -> Seems that she is still undecided...
-> I don't like animals at all!
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    The cat hisses at you and darts away.
    Tsuru: You don't? Well... That seems like something important to note.
    That... Sounded quite ominous...
Tsuru: Well, we will be leaving soon anyway.
Tsuru: You are welcome to wait here, make yourself comfortable.
There is a sudden ring, cutting through your silence.
Snail: *Bere-bere-bere-bere!*
Tsuru: Hm. I'll get that.
Tsuru: Tsuru here.
Officer: Lady Tsuru! I didn't want to interrupt you, but... We have a situation over here!
Tsuru: A situation?
-> What is their location? Can we help them?
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: Let me ask.
    Tsuru: How serious is the problem?
-> Can't you even have one day off, Tsuru?
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: This sounds serious, {$name}. Let me talk.
-> You feel disappointed but say nothing.
    Tsuru: How serious is the problem?
Officer: Well... We are trying to return to HQ with some captures we made. But three pirate vessels are blocking us and keeping us from leaving!
Officer: We have sent a distress signal to all officers of your division. But our communications could break off at any moment.
-> Blocking? Are they trying to save the captured pirates?
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru: Good question.
    Officer: They haven't made any demands yet!
-> We have to go help them.
    Tsuru: Yes. Well, at least I do.
    Tsuru: At the bare minimum, I'll have to inform the higher command and dispatch some officers.
    Tsuru: Three ships...
-> Sulk
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: Understood.
Tsuru: {$name}. I am taking this into my own hands.
Tsuru: I'm sorry, but we will need to meet another day.
-> Let me come with you!
    <<set td4_points +=1>>
    Tsuru:...
    Tsuru: I don't think that is a good idea. I noticed you were planning on having a quiet night and didn't hear the distress call.
    Tsuru: I cannot blame you, since you're not on active duty anymore...
    Tsuru: But I cannot afford to do the same.
    -> Insist!
        <<set td4_points +=1>>
        Tsuru: ...
        Tsuru: Do you truly care that much?
        Tsuru: Well, I won't keep you from doing what you must.
        Tsuru: Take your coat, {$name}. We have no time to lose.
        <<jump date_tsuru_4_on_ship>>
    -> Don't insist.
        Tsuru: Fine.
-> Say nothing.
    Tsuru: I understand it's disappointing, but...
    Tsuru: I'm afraid this can happen at any time in the Navy.
-> I guess I'll have to go with you, then...
    <<set td4_points -=1>>
    Tsuru: No. Not with that attitude.
    Tsuru: Lives are on the line, {$name}.
Tsuru: I apologize again, and will see you soon.
Tsuru leaves.
Well, that didn't go as you were expecting...
<<jump date_tsuru_4_Date_Ends_Bad>>
